    /** The resource snapshot recorded for this event and rendered at the delivery API version. object (Required): object and {@see WebhookPaymentIntentInput}. The affected public resource without expansions, client authority fields, or fields computed for an individual caller. The resource snapshot, without expansions. Webhooks omit these fields: `processing_fee_money`, `processing_fee_details`, `add_on_fees`, `merchant_net_money`, `payment_collection`, `remaining_refundable_money`. object.amount_money (Required): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount requested from the buyer, including any tip_money. Capturing doesn't change it: after a partial capture it still shows the requested amount, and captured_money shows what was collected. On a standalone payment intent, PATCH can change it only before the first confirmation attempt. An amount_money or tip_money change that leaves too little for stored splits returns LIMIT_EXCEEDED at the changed field with minimum_money. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.authorization_expires_at (Optional): string. Effective Flint deadline to capture a manual-capture hold: the earlier of the provider capture deadline and any order resource guarantee. Order guarantees last at most 24 hours from the payment attempt start and may end earlier. Capture is refused at or after this time, even while status is requires_capture. Omitted until a hold is placed. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.authorized_at (Optional): string. When the processor authorized the payment. Absent until then. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.authorized_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount the processor authorized. It always equals amount_money and doesn't change once set, even when a capture collects more. On a payment intent canceled with cancellation_reason payment_returned, it equals the authorization Flint released instead. Absent until the payment is authorized, and on payments canceled before authorization. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.cancellation_reason (Optional): string. Flint-normalized reason the payment intent was canceled. Present only while status is canceled. A cancellation without a specific reason returns payment_canceled. Absent while last_payment_error.code is payment_blocked and Flint has not identified money to return. Unknown processor values are returned as payment_canceled. Value enum: "requested_by_customer", "duplicate", "fraudulent", "abandoned", "invoice_payment_failed", "invoice_voided", "order_closed", "payment_canceled", "payment_returned". object.capturable_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of the authorization you can still capture. Positive only while status is requires_capture, and zero after you capture or cancel or the authorization expires. The authorization lapses at authorization_expires_at, and a capture attempted after that fails even if this is positive. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.capture_method (Optional): string. When money is collected. Defaults to automatic. Value enum: "automatic", "manual". object.captured_at (Optional): string. When money was captured. For automatic capture, this is when the payment succeeded. Absent until capture. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.captured_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The amount collected from the buyer, including captured_tip_money. Reconcile revenue and print receipts from this amount, not amount_money. Zero while a hold is open, and positive whenever status is succeeded. After an overcapture it is above authorized_money. Also positive on a payment intent canceled with cancellation_reason payment_returned: Flint captured the money and is returning it through a refund with reason payment_returned. processing_fee_money, merchant_net_money, and refunds are based on it. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.captured_tip_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of captured_money that is a tip: the capture's tip_money when it sent one, otherwise the tip the authorization carried, at most captured_money. tip_money keeps the tip the authorization carried. Refunds return it last. Absent until the payment is captured. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.checkout_session_id (Optional): string. Flint checkout session ID associated with this payment, when present. Example: "cs_01KEZF7C004JRWFW43H037MQRN". object.created_at (Optional): string. RFC3339 timestamp. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.customer (Optional): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput} or null. The linked customer. Returned only with expand=customer. Present only when `expand` includes `customer`; `null` when expanded and there is no related customer. object.customer.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedCustomerSummaryInput}. A customer's summary fields, returned in place of a customer ID when the customer is expanded. object.customer.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.customer_id (Optional): string. Customer linked to this payment intent. Example: "cus_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.customer_presence (Required): string. Whether the customer was present for the most recent confirmation. absent means Flint charged a saved card without them, as a merchant-initiated payment on its stored credential. Subscription renewals and automatic invoice charges are absent, and other payments are absent only when confirmed or paid with customer_presence absent. A customer who pays any of them with a card they enter makes it present. Each confirmation sets it again. Value enum: "present", "absent". object.dispute_status (Optional): string. Dispute state of this payment. none means no dispute or inquiry is open or recorded. The inquiry_ values track an issuer inquiry or early warning that isn't a chargeback. Read the dispute with GET /v1/disputes for its deadline and evidence. Value enum: "none", "inquiry_needs_response", "inquiry_under_review", "inquiry_closed", "needs_response", "under_review", "won", "lost", "prevented", "other". object.external_reference_id (Optional): string or null. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. `null` when no external reference ID has been set on the payment intent. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.failed_attempt_count (Optional): integer. All-time failed-attempt count. Present on merchant reads; omitted for buyer credentials. Format: int64. object.failed_attempts (Optional): Array of {@see FailedPaymentAttemptInput}. Newest 50 failed attempts, newest first, with merchant-only card and buyer evidence frozen at admission. Older attempts can be included in failed_attempt_count. object.failed_attempts[] (Value): {@see FailedPaymentAttemptInput}. Merchant-only evidence from one failed payment attempt. Fields absent from the original attempt are omitted. object.fulfillment_hold (Optional): {@see PaymentFulfillmentHoldInput}. Present when a payment provider asked Flint to pause fulfillment for this payment. While its status is active, open fulfillments on the order are on hold with reason payment_review. payment_intent.fulfillment_hold_updated is sent when the hold starts and when it lifts. A hold on fulfillment tied to a payment, with the reason, the action required, and whether the hold is active or released. object.idempotency_key (Optional): string or null. The Idempotency-Key of the request that created this resource. `null` when that request sent no key, Flint created the resource, the reader isn't the caller that created it (another app install, a buyer, or the merchant reading an app's or buyer's record), or the caller that created an older record is unknown. Filter its list with `idempotency_key` to find it. Recorded payloads, including replayed responses and webhook events, can return `null`. To find a key that a replay returns as `null`, read the resource. Buyer sessions on routes shared with merchants get `null`. `/v1/me` responses do not include this field. object.invoice (Optional): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput} or null. The linked invoice. Returned only with expand=invoice. Present only when `expand` includes `invoice`; `null` when expanded and there is no related invoice. object.invoice.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedInvoiceSummaryInput}. An invoice's summary fields, including status, due date, and paid, outstanding, and refunded amounts, returned when the invoice is expanded. object.invoice.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.invoice_id (Optional): string. Invoice this payment intent collects, when it pays an invoice. Example: "inv_01KEZF7C00A5GEBMWHEAJFSAR4". object.invoice_schedule_entry_id (Optional): string. The invoice installment this payment collects. Example: "invse_01KEZF7C006JCPQBD8VZ0RNT6R". object.last_payment_error (Required): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput} or null. Most recent payment error. Null when no payment error is recorded. object.last_payment_error.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see PaymentErrorSummaryInput}. A summary of why a payment attempt failed, with a normalized error code, a message, the failure time, and remediation. object.last_payment_error.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.latest_order_payment_attempt_id (Optional): string or null. The order payment attempt that most recently used this payment intent. Start times count to the second; of attempts that started in the same second, the one with the highest order_payment_attempt_id is named. `null` when no attempt has used it yet; omitted for payment intents without an order. It changes only when an attempt starts using this payment intent, which advances version. Returned with merchant credentials; omitted with buyer