e payment intent. Format: email. maxLength: 255. Example: "buyer@example.com". object.refund_expires_at (Optional): string or null. Last time Flint can refund this payment through the original payment method. A refund submitted at exactly this time is accepted; after it, refunds through the original payment method are refused. Today only Affirm has a refund window: 120 days after the payment settles. `null` when the method has no refund window, the payment has not succeeded with captured money, or its capture time is missing. Always present with merchant credentials. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.refund_status (Optional): string. How much of captured_money has been refunded, including value issued as store credit, based on refunded_money. Value enum: "none", "partially_refunded", "refunded". object.refunded_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. Total refunded against captured_money, including value issued as store credit and processor refunds still pending. Failed and canceled refunds aren't counted. Zero when nothing has been refunded. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.released_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput}. The part of the authorization returned to the buyer without being charged: the uncaptured remainder after a partial capture, or the whole authorization after a cancellation or expiry. It was never collected, so it needs no refund and can't be captured later. Zero after a capture at or above the authorization. Absent until the payment is authorized. Monetary amount represented as integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency code. object.request_overcapture (Optional): boolean. Whether one capture may collect more than the authorization where the card network allows it. Fixed at create. Always present with merchant credentials; omitted with buyer and checkout credentials. object.return_id (Optional): string. Flint return ID associated with this payment, when present. Example: "ret_01KEZF7C00PG93650ZKVQNGF7X". object.return_resolution_id (Optional): string. The return resolution whose balance this payment collects. Set for exchange balances and corrections. Example: "retres_01KEZF7C00C7RZJN31W9SGMEQ3". object.risk (Optional): {@see PaymentRiskInput} or null. Risk assessment. Always present with merchant credentials. `null` when the payment intent's latest payment attempt has no completed risk assessment, such as before its first confirmation. Omitted with the checkout credential. object.risk.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see PaymentRiskInput}. The risk assessment for a payment intent, with its risk level, score, outcome, and any matched rule or review. object.risk.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.selected_payment_option (Optional): string. The payment option the most recent confirmation used. Absent until the payment intent is first confirmed. Value enum: "card", "apple_pay", "google_pay", "affirm", "ach_debit", "card_present". object.splits (Optional): Array of {@see PaymentSplitInput}. Top-level PaymentSplit children in their current state, embedded whole. Empty when the payment has no splits. Child changes do not send payment_intent.updated. Omitted for buyer and checkout credentials. object.splits[] (Value): {@see PaymentSplitInput}. A top-level child of a payment intent dividing the collecting merchant's payment funds with one seller. Both parties read this same resource with their own credentials. object.statement_descriptor (Required): string or null. The text shown on the buyer's card or bank statement for this payment. `null` until the charge is created. `null` when the provider supplies no descriptor. Frozen when the charge is created. object.status (Required): string. Lifecycle status. requires_payment_method covers both a new payment intent and one whose last attempt failed, so read last_payment_error with it. succeeded, canceled, and expired are final. Refunds and disputes never change status. Value enum: "requires_payment_method", "requires_confirmation", "requires_action", "processing", "requires_capture", "canceled", "succeeded", "expired". object.subscription_id (Optional): string. The subscription whose billing charged this payment: its first charge, a renewal, a retry or a setup fee. Not set for the checkout payment that created a subscription. Example: "sub_01KEZF7C00BVRE8YDBXQB74BBM". object.support_reference (Required): string. Opaque payment reference to share with merchant support. Do not parse its format. object.supported_actions (Required): Array of string. Verbs this payment intent accepts now, each a POST to /v1/payment-intents/{payment_intent_id}/{action}. The list includes stored order facts and can change without a payment intent version change. Order legs list confirm when a single leg can pay the order or an open attempt can continue it. Several unpaid legs, selected gift cards, or automatic tax with a leg below the balance require pay_order instead. Invoice payments list only cancel. An unused first-period subscription payment lists cancel once the subscription is canceled. Order edit payments list confirm while awaiting payment details or action. A listed action can still be refused due to an open risk review, an order payment attempt, a closed order, or the merchant account. A managed_by_owner refusal names the owner and its command in remediation.next_actions. The merchant list is credential-independent. Checkout credentials receive that list filtered to confirm and cancel on their own session's intents, never capture. Customer sessions omit this field. New actions may be added. [] enum: "confirm", "capture", "cancel". object.supported_actions[] (Value): string.  Value enum: "confirm", "capture", "cancel". object.tip_money (Optional): {@see MoneyValueInput} or null. Portion of amount_money that is a tip. Uses amount_money's currency and is at most amount_money. `null` when no tip is set, and for an order payment until its payment attempt has moved past requires_